Recipe tuple reads
├── when ReadCached executes
│   ├── it binds full-width values and runs exactly one fresh STATICCALL
│   ├── it returns the word at the configured query offset and caches the complete response
│   ├── it preserves query index, binding, returndata and checked offset validation
│   ├── it bubbles target failures
│   └── it replaces only the previously cached response
├── when ReadWord executes
│   ├── it accepts only an earlier, latest ReadCached producer's unpacked instruction index
│   ├── it rejects self, future, absent, non-cached, packed and replaced references
│   ├── it extracts full-width words at aligned and unaligned byte offsets
│   ├── it rejects short data and retains checked offset overflow behavior
│   └── it rejects truncated instruction payloads
└── when recipes execute
    ├── cached and extracted values work in executor and account capability contexts
    ├── ordinary and conditional reads retain fresh query and lazy fallback behavior
    ├── ordinary reads and state changes do not replace immutable cached data
    ├── fresh cached reads observe changes while earlier numeric results remain usable
    ├── execution boundaries reset the cache
    ├── failed extraction rolls back prior state changes
    └── isolated gas comparisons return the same tuple values
